  "plain": "A young lawyer named Dylan Guthrie has written a law article finding that no one has been prosecuted for passing secret information to Congress through proper, secure channels. Kurt McConnell, a former Senate staffer, mentions it to Michels, saying he believes it came out in the Harvard Law Review; he does not quote it, so how far it goes is left to his summary. The point he draws is that would-be whistleblowers on UFO programs need not fear prison for speaking to Congress the right way."
